                                                "sense_id": "bee0d8a1-f3eb-3cad-a094-e11ffa7ec4b2",
                                                "text": "If you burn wood on its own, the flue gases are cooler than from a coal fire. This can result in tars condensing out within the parging and brickwork of the flue, sometimes causing brown or yellow staining on upstairs chimney breasts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
